<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - June 11.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - June 11.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	  ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Xingsuhai	 35,208   June  1    June 13    Inchon</p>
<p> Jiang Qing	42,000   June 10    June 21    Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   June 21		   Inchon</p>
<p> Jade Pacific    32,000   June 25		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Delta-Trident   35,000   June 14		   Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Venus	     39,185   June 14		   KISCO</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Nurten Ana	33,000   May  25    June 13    Kangwon</p>
<p> Quatetdla	 22,500   July 10		   POSCO</p>
<p> Caspian-Trident 38,000   July 21		   POSCO</p>
<p> Seabee1	   30,000   Mid-July		  POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Faethon	   30,000   End-June		  POSCO</p>
<p> Cupa		22,000   July 10		   POSCO</p>
<p> Feng Yao	  50,000   July 15		   POSCO</p>
<p> Al Qawiyyu	30,000   July 16		   POSCO</p>
<p> Lok Kranti	31,000   End-July		  POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Orhan Ekinci    33,474   June 17		   Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
